<article class="env-proposition" id="04QH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04QH">Proposition <span data-tag="04QH">79.12.11</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$ which is separated and locally of finite type. Then $(X/Y)_{fin}$ is an algebraic space. Moreover, the morphism $(X/Y)_{fin} \to Y$ is étale. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/04PG" data-tag="04PG">79.12.3</a> we may replace $X$ by the open subscheme which is locally quasi-finite over $Y$. Hence we may assume that $f$ is separated and locally quasi-finite. We will check the three conditions of Spaces, Definition <a href="/tag/025Y" data-tag="025Y">65.6.1</a>. Condition (1) follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/04PE" data-tag="04PE">79.12.1</a>. Condition (2) follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/04PK" data-tag="04PK">79.12.7</a>. Finally, condition (3) follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/04QG" data-tag="04QG">79.12.10</a>. Thus $(X/Y)_{fin}$ is an algebraic space. Moreover, that lemma shows that there exists a commutative diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ U \ar[rr] \ar[rd] &  &  (X/Y)_{fin} \ar[ld] \\  &  Y }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       with horizontal arrow surjective and étale and south-east arrow étale. By Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03FS" data-tag="03FS">66.16.3</a> this implies that the south-west arrow is étale as well. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>